---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const toolGroups = [
  { category: "Design / CAD", tools: ["Fusion 360", "SolidWorks"] },
  { category: "Analysis", tools: ["Python", "MATLAB", "R", "NASA CEA / RocketCEA"] },
  { category: "Manufacturing", tools: ["3D Printing / CNC"] },
  { category: "Languages", tools: ["C++"] },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About | Henry Nickless"
  description="About Henry Nickless, an aerospace engineering student at CU Boulder working on liquid rocket propulsion, telescope hardware, and astrophotography."
  image="about/headshot.jpg"
  variant="gallery"
>
  <section class="about">
    <aside class="about-side">
      <figure class="about-headshot">
        <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/about/headshot.jpg`} alt="Henry Nickless" width="900" height="1125" />
      </figure>
      <div class="about-meta mono">
        <span>Aerospace Engineering, CU Boulder</span>
        <span>Class of 2028 · Minor in Astrophysical &amp; Planetary Sciences</span>
      </div>
      <div class="about-links">
        <a class="btn" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}files/resume/Henry_Nickless_Resume.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Résumé ↗</a>
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:Henry.Nickless@Colorado.edu">Email</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://linkedin.com/in/henrynickless/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
      <div class="about-toolset">
        <span class="about-side-label mono">Toolset</span>
      <div class="skills-groups">
        {toolGroups.map((group) => (
          <div class="skills-group">
            <span class="skills-group-label mono">{group.category}</span>
            <div class="skills-strip">
              {group.tools.map((tool) => (
                <span class="skill-chip">{tool}</span>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="about-main">
      <span class="eyebrow">// Bio</span>
      <h1>About Me</h1>
      <p>
        Since my first engineering class in high school, I've been curious
        about the delicacy and precision that go into the engineering process.
        Taking apart old electronics wasn't enough to stifle that curiosity;
        it's just pulled me further into the engineering rabbit hole ever
        since.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm studying to become an aerospace engineer at the University of
        Colorado Boulder (Class of 2028), minoring in Astrophysical and
        Planetary Sciences. When I'm not studying, I'm usually playing
        volleyball or working on engineering projects, split between
        astrophotography builds and CU's Sounding Rocket Lab. I frequently
        work with other people to push ideas forward and like collaborating
        through the problems that come up along the way. Most people know me
        as a hard worker who adjusts easily to new situations.
      </p>

    <p class="pull-quote">
      "Most people know me as a hard worker who adjusts easily to new
      situations."
    </p>

    <p>
      At SRL, I work on liquid bipropellant rocket engines. On the Taipan
      engine, I verify performance calculations for a 650lbf RP-1/LOX
      engine and help redesign the injector plate under a fixed 700 psi
      chamber pressure constraint, a lot of iterative flow and combustion
      math, plus parametric trade studies using NASA's Chemical Equilibrium
      Analysis in Python. I also helped migrate our test stand software
      from Rust to C++ and got it running smoothly ahead of the upcoming
      hot fire.
    </p>

    <p>
      More recently, I've been working with a team of engineers to develop
      a regeneratively cooled liquid rocket engine capable of 2,000 lbf of
      thrust. I built a performance toolset in Python using the RocketCEA
      library to reconstruct NASA CEA data, and ran trade studies to find
      the optimal engine geometry, balancing theoretical performance
      against the physical constraints of our test stand. I'm currently
      co-developing the engine's unlike-doublet impinging injector plate
      using additive manufacturing, with an ASI and pressure sensors
      integrated directly into the design, topology-optimized to stay
      lightweight and 3D-printable.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before rockets, there was a telescope. I designed and 3D-printed a
      Newtonian telescope setup (7+ custom components, an electronic
      dew-prevention system for the mirrors, and CNC-milled focus adapters
      strong enough to carry a 5+ lb camera) all for under $30 in
      materials.
    </p>

    <p>
      I also spent a semester on a six-person team building and
      flight-testing a glider, where I engineered an elevator mechanism
      with a 20° trim range at under a gram of mass.
    </p>



    <div class="cut-line"><span>In The Field</span></div>

    <div class="field-gallery">
      <figure>
        <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/about/telescope-fieldwork.jpg`} alt="Henry Nickless setting up his Newtonian telescope at night" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="mono"><span class="fg-figno">FIG. 02</span>Telescope, in the field</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/about/glider-workshop.jpg`} alt="Henry Nickless holding the six-person team's glider in the workshop" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="mono"><span class="fg-figno">FIG. 03</span>Glider build, workshop</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/about/rocket-build.jpg`} alt="Henry Nickless fabricating a rocket engine component in the driveway" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="mono"><span class="fg-figno">FIG. 04</span>Rocket build, on the bench</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p>
      I'm looking forward to developing my skills further and meeting
      like-minded people along the way. When I'm not in the lab, I'm
      usually outside with a camera pointed at the sky. You can find some
      of that at <a href="https://instagram.com/astro.htn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@astro.htn</a>.
    </p>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 1240px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 0 3rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 340px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3.5rem;
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
    .about-side { position: static !important; max-width: 420px; }
  }
  .about-side {
    position: sticky;
    top: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .about-headshot { margin: 0; }
  .about-headshot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-500);
  }
  .about-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    color: var(--paper-dim);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .about-meta span:first-child { color: var(--paper); }
  .about-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .about-links .btn { font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem; }
  .about-side-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--redline);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .about-main { max-width: 72ch; }
  .about-main .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--redline);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    display: block;
  }
  .about-main h1 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); }
  .about p { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .about-main a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; }

  .about .skill-chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-500);
    background: var(--ink-800);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem;
  }
  .skills-groups { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; }
  .skills-group-label {
    display: block;
    color: var(--paper-dim);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .about .skills-strip { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.45rem; }

  .field-gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .field-gallery figure { margin: 0; }
  .field-gallery img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-500);
  }
  .field-gallery figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--paper-dim);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .field-gallery .fg-figno { color: var(--redline); margin-right: 0.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
</style>
